# S1.1: the same uncaught `merge`, thrown by E itself: `q: merge: P` gives q a fresh merge of P, the
# program's first merge, which the driver fails (`mergefail 1`).  E declares no throws, so its
# status is 0 + 1; the root receives 1, the entry has no value (exit 1) and the Message is
# stopped.  Completing would return 5.
P:
    size_t: p 3U
end: P

q: merge: P
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 5; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
